Installing Gimmix
=================

Requirements
------------
* GTK+ >= 2.24 and GLib >= 2.32
* libmpd >= 0.17.0
* pkg-config
* TagLib >= 1.4 with its C bindings (taglib_c), unless configured with
  --disable-tageditor
* libcurl >= 7.19.4 and json-glib >= 1.2, unless configured with both
  --disable-cover and --disable-lyrics

On Debian and Ubuntu the packages are libgtk2.0-dev, libmpd-dev,
libtagc0-dev, libcurl4-openssl-dev and libjson-glib-dev. On Gentoo they
are x11-libs/gtk+:2, media-libs/libmpd, media-libs/taglib, net-misc/curl
and dev-libs/json-glib.

Building a release
------------------
    ./configure
    make
    make install

Gimmix is installed to /usr/local by default. Pass --prefix to configure
to change that, for example ./configure --prefix=/usr.

Building from git
-----------------
A git checkout has no configure script. Generate it with

    ./autogen.sh

which needs autoconf, automake, gettext (for autopoint) and pkg-config,
and then runs configure with any arguments you pass to it. Set
NOCONFIGURE=1 to only generate the files.

Configuration
-------------
Gimmix stores its settings in ~/.gimmixrc and asks for the MPD connection
on the first start. The settings are described in the gimmix(1) manual
page and in README.
